{
	"_description": "Cross-driver corpus for erased and synthetic n-grams. A Backspace pops the newest erasable history entry and flags the n-grams that ended on it as errors (e); a Backspace never flags another Backspace. Synthetic events (meta s=1, st=hotstring|llm) carry their source into esrc and never count as the user's mistake. Each vector is replayed as one typing entry per flush, for one application, through the macOS (aggregator walk_typing) and Linux (aggregate_walker.walk with a carried context) walkers. 'expected' lists, per n-gram family, every token whose typed count c or erased count e is above zero, with c, e and the per-source counts esrc. The comparison is exact. The AHK replayer (KLW_WalkTypingEntry) is to be written on the PC; it is not part of this change.",
	"date": "2024-06-01",
	"app": "CorrectionApp",
	"timestamps": ["2024-06-01 10:00:00.000", "2024-06-01 10:00:01.000"],
